14>what is parametric and non parametric algorithm
You always use the same ingredients and same steps. That’s a parametric algorithm — it has a fixed number of rules
Parametric algorithms assume a fixed functional form for the model and learn a finite set of parameters from the training data.

That’s a non-parametric algorithm — it adjusts based on the data!
Non-parametric algorithms do not assume a fixed form. They can adapt their structure based on the data and grow in complexity with more samples.
